# Lumiere ERP — Reducer Architecture Conventions

## Core Rule

Every reducer must separate **scope/auth parameters** (flat) from **user-driven entity data** (input struct).

---

## 1) Parameter Roles

| Parameter | Type | Rule |
|-----------|------|------|
| `organization_id` | `u64` | Always flat — scopes the permission check |
| `company_id` | `u64` | Always flat — scopes tenant isolation |
| `<entity>_id` | `u64` | Always flat — identifies the target record for update/delete |
| Single-toggle booleans | `bool` | Flat is acceptable for dedicated toggle reducers (e.g. `set_*_active`) |
| All entity field values | `*Params` struct | Always in an input struct — never as individual flat params |

---

## 2) Input Struct Pattern

### Naming

```
Create<EntityName>Params   — for create reducers
Update<EntityName>Params   — for update reducers
```

### Derive

```rust
#[derive(SpacetimeType, Clone, Debug)]
pub struct CreateFooParams { ... }
```

> ⚠️ `SpacetimeType` is required for structs passed as reducer parameters.
> Do NOT use `#[table(...)]` on input structs — they are value types, not tables.

### Placement

Define all `*Params` structs in a clearly marked section **between the table definitions and the reducers** in the same file:

```rust
// ── Tables ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ... table structs ...

// ── Input Params ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ... params structs ...

// ── Reducers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ... reducers ...
```

---

## 3) No Hardcoded Values in Reducer Bodies

**Every field in the inserted/updated row must come from one of three sources:**

1. `ctx` — sender, timestamp (audit/ownership fields)
2. `params.*` — user-provided data
3. A value derived/computed from other params (not a literal)

### ❌ WRONG — hardcoded defaults polluting the reducer body

```rust
ctx.db.foo().insert(Foo {
    id: 0,
    active: true,               // hardcoded
    balance: 0.0,               // hardcoded
    line_ids: Vec::new(),       // hardcoded
    description: None,          // hardcoded
    is_required: false,         // hardcoded
    ...
});
```

### ✅ CORRECT — all field values from params

```rust
ctx.db.foo().insert(Foo {
    id: 0,                                      // auto_inc placeholder — only allowed literal
    active: params.active,
    balance: params.balance,
    line_ids: params.line_ids,
    description: params.description,
    is_required: params.is_required,
    is_root: params.parent_id.is_none(),        // derived — acceptable
    create_uid: Some(ctx.sender()),             // from ctx — acceptable
    create_date: Some(ctx.timestamp),           // from ctx — acceptable
    ...
});
```

### Allowed exceptions (only these)

| Field | Value | Reason |
|-------|-------|--------|
| `id` | `0` | SpacetimeDB auto_inc placeholder — required |
| `create_uid` / `write_uid` | `Some(ctx.sender())` | Identity comes from context |
| `create_date` / `write_date` | `Some(ctx.timestamp)` | Timestamp comes from context |
| `user_id` (ownership) | `Some(ctx.sender())` | Assigned from context, not user input |
| Derived booleans | `params.x.is_none()`, `params.x > 0`, etc. | Computed from params — not literal |

---

## 4) Reducer Signatures

### Create

```rust
#[spacetimedb::reducer]
pub fn create_foo(
    ctx: &ReducerContext,
    organization_id: u64,
    company_id: u64,
    params: CreateFooParams,
) -> Result<(), String> { ... }
```

### Update

```rust
#[spacetimedb::reducer]
pub fn update_foo(
    ctx: &ReducerContext,
    organization_id: u64,
    company_id: u64,
    foo_id: u64,
    params: UpdateFooParams,
) -> Result<(), String> { ... }
```

### Delete

```rust
#[spacetimedb::reducer]
pub fn delete_foo(
    ctx: &ReducerContext,
    organization_id: u64,
    company_id: u64,
    foo_id: u64,
) -> Result<(), String> { ... }
```

### Dedicated toggle (no params struct needed)

```rust
#[spacetimedb::reducer]
pub fn set_foo_active(
    ctx: &ReducerContext,
    organization_id: u64,
    company_id: u64,
    foo_id: u64,
    active: bool,
) -> Result<(), String> { ... }
```

---

## 5) Update Struct Field Coverage

Update params structs use `Option<T>` for every field that may change. The reducer applies only the `Some` values:

```rust
#[derive(SpacetimeType, Clone, Debug)]
pub struct UpdateFooParams {
    pub name: Option<String>,
    pub code: Option<String>,
    pub partner_id: Option<u64>,
    // ...
}
```

Fields that are system-managed and never directly updated by callers (e.g. `balance`, `line_ids`, `child_ids`) should be omitted from update params — they are mutated by dedicated domain logic inside the reducer (balance recalculation, relation management, etc.).

---

## 6) Create Struct Field Coverage

Create params structs use **non-optional types** for required fields and `Option<T>` / `Vec<T>` for optional/relational fields. They must cover **all** table columns except:

- `id` — auto_inc, omitted
- `create_uid` / `write_uid` / `create_date` / `write_date` — from ctx, omitted
- `user_id` (ownership field) — from ctx, omitted

Everything else — including fields that will commonly be initialized to `false`, `0.0`, or empty `Vec` — belongs in the params struct so the caller is explicit.

---

## 7) Company Scope Guard

Every create/update/delete reducer that touches a record owned by a company must verify ownership before mutating:

```rust
if record.company_id != company_id {
    return Err("Record does not belong to this company".to_string());
}
```

This check must come immediately after the `.find()` lookup, before any mutation.

---

## 8) Audit Log

Every reducer must call `write_audit_log_v2` (struct-based) as its final action before `Ok(())`.

### AuditLogParams fields

| Field | Type | Notes |
|-------|------|-------|
| `company_id` | `Option<u64>` | Tenant scope |
| `table_name` | `&'static str` | Snake-case table name |
| `record_id` | `u64` | ID of the mutated row |
| `action` | `&'static str` | `"CREATE"` · `"UPDATE"` · `"DELETE"` · `"SET_ACTIVE"` |
| `old_values` | `Option<String>` | JSON snapshot before mutation; `None` for creates |
| `new_values` | `Option<String>` | JSON snapshot after mutation; `None` for deletes |
| `changed_fields` | `Vec<String>` | List of field names that changed |
| `metadata` | `Option<String>` | Arbitrary JSON; `None` if unused |

Context-derived fields — **never pass these, the helper derives them automatically**:
- `session_id` — lower 64 bits of `ctx.connection_id()` (128-bit session token)
- `ip_address` — not exposed by SpacetimeDB 2.0.1 WASM sandbox; always `None`
- `user_agent` — not exposed by SpacetimeDB 2.0.1 WASM sandbox; always `None`
- `user_identity` — `ctx.sender()`
- `timestamp` — `ctx.timestamp`

### Usage

```rust
use crate::helpers::{write_audit_log_v2, AuditLogParams};

write_audit_log_v2(ctx, organization_id, AuditLogParams {
    company_id: Some(company_id),
    table_name: "my_table",
    record_id: row.id,
    action: "CREATE",
    old_values: None,
    new_values: Some(serde_json::json!({ "name": params.name }).to_string()),
    changed_fields: vec!["name".to_string()],
    metadata: None,
});
```

**Do NOT use `write_audit_log` (flat positional form) in new code** — it is deprecated.

---

## 9) Quick Checklist

Before submitting any reducer:

- [ ] Scope params (`organization_id`, `company_id`, `*_id`) are flat
- [ ] All entity field values are in a `*Params` struct
- [ ] Params struct derives `SpacetimeType, Clone, Debug`
- [ ] No hardcoded literals in the insert/update call except `id: 0`
- [ ] `create_uid`/`write_uid`/`create_date`/`write_date` come from `ctx`
- [ ] Company ownership guard present on update/delete
- [ ] `write_audit_log_v2` called before `Ok(())`
